11190	///
11191	/// Ruling of 2026-08-26 (M17.5 A05): for HAQP-1a, exhaustiveness is claimed
11192	/// over ILRP alone, every other durable transition is deferred to M17.9, and
11193	/// the split is declared in the packet rather than left implicit. Deciding
11194	/// which of the runtime's transitions are *registrable* boundaries is runtime
11195	/// design work; doing it here would either block 1a on Phase 1 or pass by
11196	/// picking a convenient definition, and ADR-0020 §3 forbids improvising
11197	/// qualification semantics.
