11199	/// What is enforced instead is that the disclosure stays true. A prose scope
11200	/// note rots the first time somebody adds a commit site — which is exactly the
11201	/// defect A05 found in the original unscoped claim — so every durable
11202	/// transition in tracked source must fall inside a declared in-scope subsystem
11203	/// or a declared deferred surface, with counts matching exactly. A new
11204	/// `txn.commit()` anywhere turns the packet red until it is either registered
11205	/// or disclosed.
11206	fn verify_crash_boundary_scope(root: &Utf8Path, packet: &Packet) -> Result<()> {
